WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.120
[Narrator] Netflix has
released the final trailer

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.290
for season three of "Stranger Things."

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:07.840
It seems to confirm a possible fan theory

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:09.849
about the season's main villain

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:11.790
and includes more pop-culture references

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.910
from the '80s and early '90s.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.630
Here are 11 details you might have missed.

00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.070
First off, the trailer release.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.030
The trailer came out at 7:11
p.m. Pacific Standard Time.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:30.482
Perhaps the 7 is because the
new season debuts in July,

00:00:30.482 --> 00:00:31.998
and 11 after...

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.931
Well, that seems obvious.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:38.890
The trailer is set to the song
"Confrontation and Rescue,"

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:42.864
a Philip Glass song from the 1980s.

00:00:42.864 --> 00:00:44.511
Eleven: It's building something.

00:00:45.702 --> 00:00:48.482
[Narrator] The trailer starts
with an ominous voiceover.

00:00:48.482 --> 00:00:49.315
Mind Flayer: You

00:00:50.756 --> 00:00:51.739
let us in.

00:00:52.723 --> 00:00:55.240
[Narrator] There's a good
chance this is the Mind Flayer,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.673
aka the Shadow Monster,

00:00:57.673 --> 00:01:01.531
who we first saw in season
two, which possessed Will,

00:01:01.531 --> 00:01:03.931
taking a new human form.

00:01:03.931 --> 00:01:06.997
Could it be Mayor Kline,
played by Cary Elwes?

00:01:06.997 --> 00:01:08.950
Or could it be Billy?

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.780
More on that in a bit.

00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:13.359
This all suggests that
while Eleven supposedly

00:01:13.359 --> 00:01:16.720
closed the gate to the Upside
Down in the season two finale,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.950
something ended up staying behind.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.650
Will: What if he never left?

00:01:23.565 --> 00:01:25.043
[Narrator] In another shot,

00:01:25.043 --> 00:01:27.677
we see the gang preparing for a showdown.

00:01:27.677 --> 00:01:29.493
We see Jonathan grab an ax

00:01:29.493 --> 00:01:31.301
and Nancy cocking a gun.

00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:34.740
Nancy is first seen with a
handgun back in season one.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:37.290
She and Jonathan are
practicing in a field.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:39.300
Nancy proves to be a natural,

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:41.570
hitting a can with her first shot.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:44.660
Jonathan isn't so lucky,
which is maybe why he choose

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:46.770
to use an ax as a weapon.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.243
She also carries a gun in season two.

00:01:51.013 --> 00:01:53.717
We see Lucas inside the Starcourt Mall

00:01:53.717 --> 00:01:55.640
practicing with a slingshot.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:58.300
Slingshots are Lucas' weapon of choice.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.570
In the season one finale, he
uses one against the Demogorgon

00:02:01.570 --> 00:02:05.045
and actually gets a shot
in, with Eleven's help.

00:02:08.897 --> 00:02:11.783
And speaking of the mall, as
we saw in the first trailer,

00:02:11.783 --> 00:02:14.380
it will be a major
setting in season three.

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.673
In the background you'll spot
a number of 1980s brand logos,

00:02:17.673 --> 00:02:19.547
including Burger King,

00:02:19.547 --> 00:02:21.064
The Gap,

00:02:21.064 --> 00:02:22.822
JCPenney,

00:02:22.822 --> 00:02:24.322
and Orange Julius.

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:28.450
At the carnival, if you look closely,

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:30.806
you can see an old-school Coke logo.

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:34.940
At one point, we get a
quick glimpse of Will's arm.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:38.628
On his wrist is a 1980s
Nelsonic Q-bert game watch.

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.284
As always, the show pays homage

00:02:43.284 --> 00:02:46.430
to a lot of beloved pop
culture of the 1980s,

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.280
and this time the 1990s as well.

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:52.570
The Duffer brothers cited
1993's "Jurassic Park"

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:55.270
as a major influence on season three.

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.920
Some of the shots at the
mall are clear references

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:01.598
to this scene in which Tim and
Lex are hiding in the kitchen

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:03.183
from the velociraptors.

00:03:04.418 --> 00:03:06.780
Speaking of early '90s references,

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:09.052
this new evil-looking
character is giving off

00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:12.745
T-1000 vibes from 1991's "Terminator 2."

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:17.100
You might recognize him
as the guy with the gun

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.100
roaming through the hall of
mirrors in the previous trailer.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:23.062
There's a brief shot of Billy's car

00:03:23.062 --> 00:03:24.853
speeding towards the mall,

00:03:24.853 --> 00:03:27.403
which seems to be a mirror
image of this DeLorean scene

00:03:27.403 --> 00:03:29.119
in "Back to the Future."

00:03:29.119 --> 00:03:33.280
This film was released in
1985, when season three is set,

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.010
and the scene happens to include

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:38.786
the same vintage JCPenney
logo we mentioned earlier.

00:03:40.902 --> 00:03:44.460
At one point, we get another
glimpse of the Mind Flayer.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:47.600
If you recall, in the
final shot of season two,

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.930
this creature was seen hovering
over Hawkins Middle School.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.182
There also seems to be
hints that the Mind Flayer

00:03:53.182 --> 00:03:55.600
will take another human form this season.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:58.780
The question is who will
be the host this time?

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:01.160
Fans are speculating
that it could be Billy,

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:03.340
and this trailer is giving
us a few major hints

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:04.750
that this is true.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.380
Will speculates that the monster

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.810
will attach itself to someone again.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:12.158
As he says this, there's
a flash of the Mind Flayer

00:04:12.158 --> 00:04:14.490
and an immediate cut to Billy.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.810
Seconds later, we get a close-up shot

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.390
of Billy's dilating pupil.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:20.270
The Brimborn Steel Works building

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:22.180
is also swarming with rats,

00:04:22.180 --> 00:04:24.760
which tend to symbolize
some sort of outbreak,

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:27.181
so clearly someone is
going to be infected.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:29.610
Was there anything we missed?

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:31.618
Let us know in the comments.

